{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","text":"Hypergraph"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edge position ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in index","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a per-incidence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" shifted by n, and of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traversal"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Connectivity"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPaths"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidentIndexRows"},{"type":"text","text":" writes the view’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows out once per call from the base’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidenceRows"},{"type":"text","text":", in O(n + m + p), for whole-graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range, O(1). On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its incidences, every read is O(1) plus"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the row. On any other base, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" binary-search the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedge and find the member by its rank ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)"},{"type":"text","text":"), O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" finds its place in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them on a base without a faster "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraphView, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"text":" gives the bipartite structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the view’s components restricted to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"text":" are the hypergraph’s.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"IncidenceGraphView","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs18